 rd.Screen 1 nm.	Users can construct their own Help screens, as follows:
	Each Help screen consists of 20 lines, maximum 78 characters per line,
each line ending with a carriage return and line feed. Anything can be placed
within the screen, but obviously good screen design makes for ease of use.
		 rd.New Help screens must be added at the end of this one.

	Blank lines are useful. Lines beginning with << are ignored altogether.
			Tabs are represented by ú and occupy only a single character.
	Colours: the "words" rd. bl. gn. yl. nm. (each preceded by a space) begin
red, blue, green, yellow, and normal within each line independently:  allow 10
characters for each of these 4-character words. The line beginning "	Any"
has 78 characters (tab has one; red and normal each have ten).

	Any character that rd. begins nm. a line can be found by pressing
it from within a Help screen.
Thus, pressing T will bring this line (and other similar lines in subsequent
screens) to the top of the screen.

The ability to bring a character to the top of the screen makes it convenient
to devote a single screen to a specific character for which help is required.
